---
description: Put throwaway scripts and dumps in gitignored tmp/
alwaysApply: true
---

# Scratch / temp files

- Put one-off query scripts, stdout dumps, and other throwaway files in `tmp/` (gitignored).
- Never create `tmp-*`, `tmp-out*`, or similar scratch files in the repo root.
- Do not commit anything under `tmp/`.
- Durable scripts belong in `scripts/`; lasting notes/docs belong in an intentional tracked path (e.g. `.agents/` or `docs/`), not `tmp/`.
- Prefer existing tools (`npx supabase`, npm scripts) over new one-off scripts when they already cover the need.
- When finished with a throwaway, delete it or leave it in `tmp/` — do not leave scratch files in the root or `lib/`.
